internal/setupcmd/cmd.go` `Command`, build the func from the existing `github.GhFallback` (`internal/github/ghcli.go`, uses `gh auth token --hostname github.com`) or a PAT `TokenAuth` from `github.AuthFromEnv` when the configured auth is a PAT. Reuse what #302 already put in `internal/github/auth.go`; do not add a second token reader. If the configured auth is the App, use the gh fallback.\n9-3. **Embedded workflow.** New directory `internal/setupcmd/workflow/` (new) with `bot-commits.yml`, a byte-for-byte copy of `.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml` (copying into a new path is allowed; do not edit `.github/`). New `internal/setupcmd/workflow.go`: `//go:embed workflow/bot-commits.yml` into `var botCommitsWorkflow []byte`, `const workflowPath = \".github/workflows/bot-commits.yml\"`, and `PrintWorkflow(w io.Writer) error` writing the bytes.\n10-4. **Workflow check row.** In `workflow.go` add `func checkWorkflow(ctx, fileAt func(ctx, rev, path string) ([]byte, bool, error)) Row` (name `workflow`). Absent on `origin/main` gives `StatusManual` with detail `commit .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml: run ard setup --print-workflow > .github/workflows/bot-commits.yml, then open a PR`. Different bytes (compare after normalising CRLF to LF) gives `StatusManual`, with the same fix and \"differs from the copy embedded in ard\". Equal gives `StatusOK`. If `origin/main` does not exist, give a `StatusManual` row saying it could not be checked (fetch first), never a hard failure. Add `Deps.WorkflowAt func(ctx context.Context) ([]byte, bool, error)` (new) in `internal/setupcmd/setup.go`; wire it in `cmd.go` with `gitx.New(\"\").FileAt(ctx, root, \"origin/main\", workflowPath, 1<<20)` (`internal/gitx/local.go`). Append the row in `Run` after the policy rows, before the label step, only when `WorkflowAt != nil`. Setup never commits and never writes `.github/`.\n11-5. **ARD_BOT_LOGIN row and apply.** In `internal/setupcmd/setup.go` add `Deps.Variables VariableWriter` (new interface `Set