dle it first, before config load, repo resolution or any credentials: `return PrintWorkflow(e.Stdout)`. Nothing else may be written to stdout in that mode, so a redirect to a file is clean.\n14-8. **Docs.** Update `docs/proposal.md` paragraph \"`ard setup` applies `.ard/` to GitHub\" (add the `--print-workflow` flag, confirm-before-overwrite and the manual rows), `docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md` (steps 49 and 50: use `ard setup --print-workflow` and let setup set the variable), `docs/site/getting-started.md` line 61, and `internal/initcmd/body.go` lines 64 to 65 only if the wording should mention `ard setup`. If you change `body.go`, update the matching string checks in `internal/initcmd/initcmd_test.go`. Add the `workflow/` directory to `docs/layout.md` under `internal/setupcmd/`.\n15-\n16-### Network inputs\n17-\n18-None.\n19-\n20-### Test plan\n21-\n22-Command: `make lint test` (`go vet`, gofmt check, `go test ./...`). No network; use the GitHub fake (`internal/github/fake`) and fake writers.\n23-\n24-- `internal/setupcmd/setup_test.go`:\n25-  - `TestBotLoginAbsentIsSet`: no variable, identity `ard-x[bot]`; expect one `SetRepoVariable(\"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\",\"ard-x[bot]\")` and a `changed` row.\n26-  - `TestBotLoginEqualNoWrite`: same value; expect ok and no write.\n27-  - `TestBotLoginDifferentAsksFirst`: different value, `Confirm` returns true; expect one write. With false or nil `Confirm`: no write, manual row with the `gh variable set` command.\n28-  - `TestBotLoginCheckOnly`: `--check` with drift: no write, `HasDrift` true.\n29-  - `TestBotLoginDryRun`: dry-run writer logs, row says would set.\n30-  - `TestBotLoginNotABot`: identity login with no `[bot]` suffix gives a manual row and no write.\n31-  - `TestBotLoginNeverFromConfig`: value written is exactly the identity login whatever config says.\n32-  - `TestBotLoginNoToken`: writer returns `ErrNoOperatorToken`; row is manual, run does not abort, labels still sync.\n33-  - `TestBotLoginForbiddenRead`: `GetVariable` returns `ErrForbidden`; manual row.\n34-- `internal/setupcmd/workflow_test.go` (new):\n35-  - `TestEmbeddedWorkflowMatchesRepo`: embedded bytes equal `../../.github/workflows/bot-commits.yml`, so the copy cannot drift (same relative path as `internal/botcheck/botcheck_test.go`).\n36-  - `TestCheckWorkflow`: table of absent, identical, CRLF-only difference (ok), edited (manual), `origin/main` missing (manual, not an error).\n37-  - `TestPrintWorkflow`: output equals the embedded bytes exactly.\n38-- `internal/effects/variable_test.go` (new): `Live.SetRepoVariable` against `httptest` server: create on 404, update on 200, bad repo and bad name rejected, token absent gives `ErrNoOperatorToken`, token never appears in logs; `DryRun` records `SetRepoVariable` in the ledger and makes no call.\n39-- `internal/cli/commands_test.go`: `--print-workflow` parses; with `--check` or `--create-gh-app` it is rejected.\n40-- `internal/setupcmd/cmd_test.go`: `--print-workflow` works with no config, no repo and no credentials, and writes only the workflow to stdout.\n41-- Edge cases: workflow file larger than the cap (error becomes a manual row); variable value with surrounding whitespace is compared trimmed.\n42-\n43-### Risk","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018kzKmH3nqKrvnsouCqfoWr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
